\section{Family and method}{

\code{family} is \code{"response"} (the profile is predicted and scored under the
value set; any country works) or \code{"direct"} (the utility is predicted on
the scale of one value set). \code{method} is one of \code{"R06_mvop_dim"} and
\code{"R09_chain"} (response) or \code{"D03_clad"} and \code{"D12_klapproth"} (direct);
short aliases (\code{"R06"}, \code{"mvop"}, \code{"chain"}, \code{"clad"}, \code{"klapproth"}) are
accepted. With neither argument the default response method
(\code{"R06_mvop_dim"}) is used; with \code{family} only, that family's default
(\code{"D03_clad"} for direct); with \code{method} only, the family follows from the
method; with both, they must agree.
}

\section{Predictor set}{

Each method uses its preferred predictor set among those the data support
(items, T-scores, pain intensity and age/sex; see \code{\link[=p2e_columns]{p2e_columns()}}). \code{set}
forces one of \code{"S1"} to \code{"S4"}. The chosen set is reported in a message and
in the result. The package ships no PROMIS T-score conversion table: T-score
sets need T-score columns or a \code{tscore_table} (see \code{\link[=p2e_tscores]{p2e_tscores()}}).
}

